<p>They were given the opportunity to purchase the Edison Agency in Mandan from her stepfather, C. G. Conyne, who found that phonograph music did not mix well with his watch sales and repair business. They obtained the rights from the Columbia and Victor music companies to carry their phonographs and opened their music store in the Hotel Nigey, later the McDonald Hotel, in the fall of 1918. Their store sold phonographs, records, sheet music, and player pianos, and later added other instruments. Mrs. Dahners demonstrated music by playing selections on the piano.</p>

